                <pb facs="0955" n="861" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg861"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr. Terrell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-08-21"><hi rendition="#italic">August 21,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1069.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 941, of the 6th
                    instant, and have to approve your caution in sending a telegram to each American
                    mission in the interior of Turkey requesting information as to the measure of
                    its present and future protection.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
